7176+ 7D1A              ;58) sends abort command (in order to abort existing command and get unstuck)
7177+ 7D1A              ;send_ftp_command is the main routine that sends command+ string if needed and returns ftp answer code
7178+ 7D1A              ;IN=A=0=command only (eg. "ABORT"). A=1=comamnd+prepared string from INPUT (eg. "STOR filename"), A=2=command+new INPUT
7179+ 7D1A              ;OUT=A=0=NC=sent ok, awaited ftp code returned correctly
7180+ 7D1A              ;A=1=C=c=1=error sending string
7181+ 7D1A              ;A=2=C=c=11=error in module answer (expected answer ">" not returned)
7182+ 7D1A              ;A=3=C=c=4=sent ok, but return code other than expected
